# Security & data access (always)

When adding or changing features, **preserve and extend** the patterns in `docs/AUDIT-CHECKLIST.md` and `docs/SECURITY.md`. Scan the **whole change**, not only the files you touched.

## Auth & Server Actions

- `"use server"` modules export **FormData (or similar) mutations only**.
- Mutations call `requireUser()` (or `auth()`) and use **`user.id` from the session** — never trust a client-supplied `userId`.
- Queries / services that take `userId` live in `*-data.ts` (or plain server modules) — **not** in `"use server"` files.
- Internal writers (`insertTransactionForUser`, migrate/EMI helpers, cashflow) stay out of Server Action surfaces; call them only from authenticated actions/API routes.

## Authorization

- Every mutation: `and(eq(...id), eq(...userId, user.id))` (or equivalent).
- Before ledger side effects (bank/card balances), assert owned FKs (`assertOwnedTransactionInputs` or the same pattern for the domain).
- Prefer `.returning()` / existence checks so side effects do not run on 0-row updates.

## Input & errors

- Prefer Zod (`form-schemas.ts` / action schemas) for new FormData and API bodies.
- Throw `UserFacingError` for expected validation failures; clients use `clientErrorMessage` (never raw DB/driver stacks).
- Secrets only via `getEnv()` / `EnvKeys` — never `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` for DB/auth secrets.

## Performance / DoS (security-adjacent)

- Bound lists: pagination, cursors, or caps (`TRANSACTIONS_*`, `EXPORT_MAX_ROWS`, lookbacks).
- Keep **reads pure** — no migrate/EMI/posting inside list/detail helpers; use `ensureCardLedgerSynced` (or a similar cached sync) at a single entry point if needed.
- Avoid N+1 and duplicate nested loaders (reuse preloaded data / `buildNetWorth`-style aggregators).

## Auth surfaces

- Public signup stays gated (`allowPublicSignup` / invite); production default closed.
- Rate-limit new auth-like endpoints (shared `takeRateLimit` / Redis path).
- Secrets compares: `secureStringEqual` where timing matters (invite codes, tokens).

## PWA / proxy / headers

- User HTML caches: session-scoped or purge on login/logout; do not cache APIs.
- Proxy: only real static extensions bypass auth — not `pathname.includes(".")`.
- Do not weaken CSP / security headers in `next.config.ts` without a documented reason.

## Before finishing a feature

1. Re-read this rule + relevant AUDIT items for regressions.
2. Run `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm test` (or `npm run ci`).
3. If the change adds a new pattern, update `docs/SECURITY.md` or the audit checklist in the same PR.
